<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:content="http://purl.org/rss/1.0/modules/content/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/"><channel><title>News from Google</title><link>https://blog.google/</link><description>News from Google</description><atom:link href="https://blog.google/rss/" rel="self"/><language>en-us</language><lastBuildDate>Tue, 04 Aug 2026 13:00:00 +0000</lastBuildDate><image><url>https://blog.google/static/blogv2/images/google.png</url><title>News from Google</title><link>https://blog.google/</link></image><item><title>The latest AI news we announced in July 2026</title><link>https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/technology/ai/google-ai-updates-july-2026/</link><media:content height="540" medium="image" url="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-uniblog-publish-prod/images/July_AI_Recap_still.max-600x600.format-webp.webp" width="540"/><media:description>July AI recap header</media:description><description>&lt;img src="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-uniblog-publish-prod/images/July_AI_Recap_still.max-600x600.format-webp.webp"&gt;Here are Google’s latest AI updates from July 2026</description><pubDate>Tue, 04 Aug 2026 13:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/technology/ai/google-ai-updates-july-2026/</guid><category>Search</category><category>Android</category><category>Google DeepMind</category><category>Google Workspace</category><category>Google Cloud</category><category>AI</category><category>Gemini models</category><og xmlns:og="http://ogp.me/ns#"><type>article</type><title>The latest AI news we announced in July 2026</title><description>Here are Google’s latest AI updates from July 2026</description><site_name>Google</site_name><url>https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/technology/ai/google-ai-updates-july-2026/</url></og><author xmlns:author="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><name>News from Google Team</name><title/><department/><company/></author></item><item><title>Welcome to Sail Tower, our newest Austin office</title><link>https://blog.google/company-news/inside-google/company-announcements/austin-office-sail-tower/</link><media:content height="540" medium="image" url="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-uniblog-publish-prod/images/Austin_mural_thumbnail.max-600x600.format-webp.webp" width="540"/><media:description>Austin mural</media:description><description>&lt;img src="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-uniblog-publish-prod/images/Austin_mural_thumbnail.max-600x600.format-webp.webp"&gt;Our new Austin office, Sail Tower, features flexible workspace for Googlers and a Google.org nonprofit venue for community members.</description><pubDate>Mon, 03 Aug 2026 16:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.google/company-news/inside-google/company-announcements/austin-office-sail-tower/</guid><category>Company announcements (DEPRECATED)</category><og xmlns:og="http://ogp.me/ns#"><type>article</type><title>Welcome to Sail Tower, our newest Austin office</title><description>Our new Austin office, Sail Tower, features flexible workspace for Googlers and a Google.org nonprofit venue for community members.</description><site_name>Google</site_name><url>https://blog.google/company-news/inside-google/company-announcements/austin-office-sail-tower/</url></og><author xmlns:author="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><name>Scott Foster</name><title>Vice President</title><department>Real Estate &amp; Workplace Services</department><company/></author></item><item><title>Inside our 353,000-person vibe coding course</title><link>https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/technology/developers-tools/ai-agents-intensive-recap-2026/</link><media:content height="540" medium="image" url="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-uniblog-publish-prod/images/Vibe_coding_course_hero.max-600x600.format-webp.webp" width="540"/><media:description>Illustrations of a laptop, an AI spark, messages, code, and a 3-D cube</media:description><description>&lt;img src="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-uniblog-publish-prod/images/Vibe_coding_course_hero.max-600x600.format-webp.webp"&gt;Kaggle’s AI Agents Intensive with Google brought learners together in a no-cost course to build and deploy the next frontier of AI.</description><pubDate>Mon, 03 Aug 2026 15:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/technology/developers-tools/ai-agents-intensive-recap-2026/</guid><category>Gemini models</category><category>Google Cloud</category><category>Developer tools</category><category>AI</category><og xmlns:og="http://ogp.me/ns#"><type>article</type><title>Inside our 353,000-person vibe coding course</title><description>Kaggle’s AI Agents Intensive with Google brought learners together in a no-cost course to build and deploy the next frontier of AI.</description><site_name>Google</site_name><url>https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/technology/developers-tools/ai-agents-intensive-recap-2026/</url></og><author xmlns:author="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><name>Anant Nawalgaria</name><title>Group AI Product Manager, Founder of GenAI intensive</title><department/><company/></author><author xmlns:author="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><name>Brenda Flynn</name><title>Partnerships Lead</title><department>Kaggle</department><company/></author></item><item><title>Simplify your morning with this vibe-coded schedule app.</title><link>https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/models-and-research/gemini-models/glanceboard-gemini-flash-nano-banana/</link><media:content height="540" medium="image" url="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-uniblog-publish-prod/images/Glanceboard_socialshare.max-600x600.format-webp.webp" width="540"/><description>&lt;img src="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-uniblog-publish-prod/images/Glanceboard_socialshare.max-600x600.format-webp.webp"&gt;Tired of starting your morning staring at bright screens and stressful notifications? Raph, a creative technologist at Google, built a custom app called Glanceboard with…</description><pubDate>Fri, 31 Jul 2026 19:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/models-and-research/gemini-models/glanceboard-gemini-flash-nano-banana/</guid><category>Gemini models</category><og xmlns:og="http://ogp.me/ns#"><type>article</type><title>Simplify your morning with this vibe-coded schedule app.</title><description/><site_name>Google</site_name><url>https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/models-and-research/gemini-models/glanceboard-gemini-flash-nano-banana/</url></og></item><item><title>Find out what’s new in the Gemini app in July's Gemini Drop.</title><link>https://blog.google/products-and-platforms/products/gemini/gemini-drop-july-2026/</link><media:content height="540" medium="image" url="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-uniblog-publish-prod/images/Gemini_Drops_Social.max-600x600.format-webp.webp" width="540"/><description>&lt;img src="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-uniblog-publish-prod/images/Gemini_Drops_Social.max-600x600.format-webp.webp"&gt;Gemini Drops is our regular monthly update on how to get the most out of the Gemini app.</description><pubDate>Fri, 31 Jul 2026 16:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.google/products-and-platforms/products/gemini/gemini-drop-july-2026/</guid><category>Gemini App</category><og xmlns:og="http://ogp.me/ns#"><type>article</type><title>Find out what’s new in the Gemini app in July's Gemini Drop.</title><description/><site_name>Google</site_name><url>https://blog.google/products-and-platforms/products/gemini/gemini-drop-july-2026/</url></og></item><item><title>Experience the magic of Kosovo from anywhere with Street View</title><link>https://blog.google/products-and-platforms/products/maps/google-street-view-kosovo/</link><media:content height="540" medium="image" url="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-uniblog-publish-prod/images/Kosovo_Hero_image.max-600x600.format-webp.webp" width="540"/><media:description>A stone bridge near several buildings</media:description><description>&lt;img src="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-uniblog-publish-prod/images/Kosovo_Hero_image.max-600x600.format-webp.webp"&gt;Google Maps brings Street View to Kosovo, offering a virtual tour of its vibrant cities, UNESCO World Heritage site, and natural beauty.</description><pubDate>Fri, 31 Jul 2026 08:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.google/products-and-platforms/products/maps/google-street-view-kosovo/</guid><category>Maps</category><og xmlns:og="http://ogp.me/ns#"><type>article</type><title>Experience the magic of Kosovo from anywhere with Street View</title><description>Google Maps brings Street View to Kosovo, offering a virtual tour of its vibrant cities, UNESCO World Heritage site, and natural beauty.</description><site_name>Google</site_name><url>https://blog.google/products-and-platforms/products/maps/google-street-view-kosovo/</url></og><author xmlns:author="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><name>Songran Jang</name><title>Senior Program Manager, Google Street View</title><department/><company/></author></item><item><title>Gemini Spark now integrates with Chrome</title><link>https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/products/gemini-app/gemini-spark-updates-july-2026/</link><media:content height="540" medium="image" url="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-uniblog-publish-prod/images/Blog_Header_2784x1566_Option_1.max-600x600.format-webp.webp" width="540"/><media:description>Gemini Spark integrated with Chrome</media:description><description>&lt;img src="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-uniblog-publish-prod/images/Blog_Header_2784x1566_Option_1.max-600x600.format-webp.webp"&gt;An overview of the latest Gemini Spark updates, including new Chrome web browsing capabilities.</description><pubDate>Thu, 30 Jul 2026 20:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/products/gemini-app/gemini-spark-updates-july-2026/</guid><category>Gemini App</category><og xmlns:og="http://ogp.me/ns#"><type>article</type><title>Gemini Spark now integrates with Chrome</title><description>An overview of the latest Gemini Spark updates, including new Chrome web browsing capabilities.</description><site_name>Google</site_name><url>https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/products/gemini-app/gemini-spark-updates-july-2026/</url></og><author xmlns:author="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><name>Adam Coimbra</name><title>Director, Product Management</title><department>Gemini app</department><company/></author><author xmlns:author="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><name>Charmaine Dsilva</name><title>Senior Director, Product Management</title><department/><company/></author></item><item><title>Introducing Gemini Robotics ER 2</title><link>https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/models-and-research/google-deepmind/gemini-robotics-er-2/</link><media:content height="540" medium="image" url="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-uniblog-publish-prod/images/gemini-robotics-2__blog__cover.max-600x600.format-webp.webp" width="540"/><media:description>Two robots: Duo and Apollo</media:description><description>&lt;img src="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-uniblog-publish-prod/images/gemini-robotics-2__blog__cover.max-600x600.format-webp.webp"&gt;Gemini Robotics ER 2 is a step change in video understanding, tool orchestration, and multi-robot collaboration for robotic applications.</description><pubDate>Thu, 30 Jul 2026 15:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/models-and-research/google-deepmind/gemini-robotics-er-2/</guid><category>Gemini models</category><category>Google DeepMind</category><category>Developer tools</category><og xmlns:og="http://ogp.me/ns#"><type>article</type><title>Introducing Gemini Robotics ER 2</title><description>Gemini Robotics ER 2 is a step change in video understanding, tool orchestration, and multi-robot collaboration for robotic applications.</description><site_name>Google</site_name><url>https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/models-and-research/google-deepmind/gemini-robotics-er-2/</url></og><author xmlns:author="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><name>Steven Hansen</name><title>Senior Staff Software Engineer</title><department/><company/></author><author xmlns:author="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><name>Peng Xu</name><title>Staff Software Engineer</title><department/><company/></author></item><item><title>Take a look at short films created by our latest group of artists in Google’s Flow Sessions program.</title><link>https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/models-and-research/google-labs/google-flow-sessions-short-films/</link><media:content height="540" medium="image" url="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-uniblog-publish-prod/images/Flow_social_A.max-600x600.format-webp.webp" width="540"/><description>&lt;img src="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-uniblog-publish-prod/images/Flow_social_A.max-600x600.format-webp.webp"&gt;We’re sharing a look at the short films created by our latest group of artists in Google’s Flow Sessions program.</description><pubDate>Thu, 30 Jul 2026 15:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/models-and-research/google-labs/google-flow-sessions-short-films/</guid><category>Google Labs</category><og xmlns:og="http://ogp.me/ns#"><type>article</type><title>Take a look at short films created by our latest group of artists in Google’s Flow Sessions program.</title><description/><site_name>Google</site_name><url>https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/models-and-research/google-labs/google-flow-sessions-short-films/</url></og></item><item><title>Transform any place with Nano Banana in Google Earth</title><link>https://blog.google/products-and-platforms/products/earth/nano-banana-google-earth-image-generation/</link><media:content height="540" medium="image" url="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-uniblog-publish-prod/images/Hero_Image_Wide_1.max-600x600.format-webp.webp" width="540"/><media:description>A hero image with example queries is shown.</media:description><description>&lt;img src="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-uniblog-publish-prod/images/Hero_Image_Wide_1.max-600x600.format-webp.webp"&gt;Custom images — generated from Google Earth satellite, aerial, and 3D imagery — help you redesign any location.</description><pubDate>Thu, 30 Jul 2026 12:30:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.google/products-and-platforms/products/earth/nano-banana-google-earth-image-generation/</guid><category>Google Earth</category><og xmlns:og="http://ogp.me/ns#"><type>article</type><title>Transform any place with Nano Banana in Google Earth</title><description>Custom images — generated from Google Earth satellite, aerial, and 3D imagery — help you redesign any location.</description><site_name>Google</site_name><url>https://blog.google/products-and-platforms/products/earth/nano-banana-google-earth-image-generation/</url></og><author xmlns:author="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><name>Bryan Horowitz</name><title>Product Manager</title><department>Google Earth</department><company/></author></item><item><title>How the Head of YouTube Health handles screen time with his kids</title><link>https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/technology/families/kids-summer-screen-time-tips/</link><media:content height="540" medium="image" url="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-uniblog-publish-prod/images/Screentime_Hero.max-600x600.format-webp.webp" width="540"/><media:description>Colorful illustration of two smiling parents and a child holding a tablet.</media:description><description>&lt;img src="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-uniblog-publish-prod/images/Screentime_Hero.max-600x600.format-webp.webp"&gt;Hear from Dr. Garth Graham on how he sets rules in his own home and helpful approaches for communicating about screen time.</description><pubDate>Wed, 29 Jul 2026 16:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/technology/families/kids-summer-screen-time-tips/</guid><category>Families</category><category>YouTube</category><og xmlns:og="http://ogp.me/ns#"><type>article</type><title>How the Head of YouTube Health handles screen time with his kids</title><description>Hear from Dr. Garth Graham on how he sets rules in his own home and helpful approaches for communicating about screen time.</description><site_name>Google</site_name><url>https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/technology/families/kids-summer-screen-time-tips/</url></og><author xmlns:author="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><name>Joel Meares</name><title>Contributor</title><department/><company/></author></item><item><title>We’re launching Lyria 3.5 in Google Flow Music, with advances across musicality, lyrics, vocals, and creative control.</title><link>https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/models-and-research/google-labs/lyria-3-5/</link><media:content height="540" medium="image" url="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-uniblog-publish-prod/images/Lyria3.5_social.max-600x600.format-webp.webp" width="540"/><description>&lt;img src="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-uniblog-publish-prod/images/Lyria3.5_social.max-600x600.format-webp.webp"&gt;Our newest music generation model, Lyria 3.5, delivers significant advancements across musicality, lyrics, and vocal quality, empowering you to craft richer tracks. We’r…</description><pubDate>Wed, 29 Jul 2026 16:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/models-and-research/google-labs/lyria-3-5/</guid><category>Google DeepMind</category><category>Google Labs</category><og xmlns:og="http://ogp.me/ns#"><type>article</type><title>We’re launching Lyria 3.5 in Google Flow Music, with advances across musicality, lyrics, vocals, and creative control.</title><description/><site_name>Google</site_name><url>https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/models-and-research/google-labs/lyria-3-5/</url></og></item><item><title>Prepare for the holiday season with July’s Demand Gen Drop.</title><link>https://blog.google/products/ads-commerce/demand-gen-drop-july-2026/</link><media:content height="540" medium="image" url="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-uniblog-publish-prod/images/Demand_Gen_Drops_July.max-600x600.format-webp.webp" width="540"/><description>&lt;img src="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-uniblog-publish-prod/images/Demand_Gen_Drops_July.max-600x600.format-webp.webp"&gt;Prepare for the holiday season with upgraded tROAS bidding, Checkout Links, and more from YouTube’s July Demand Gen Drop.</description><pubDate>Wed, 29 Jul 2026 15:30:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.google/products/ads-commerce/demand-gen-drop-july-2026/</guid><category>Google Ads</category><category>YouTube</category><og xmlns:og="http://ogp.me/ns#"><type>article</type><title>Prepare for the holiday season with July’s Demand Gen Drop.</title><description/><site_name>Google</site_name><url>https://blog.google/products/ads-commerce/demand-gen-drop-july-2026/</url></og></item><item><title>Gemini for macOS adds new natural language capabilities</title><link>https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/products/gemini-app/speak-naturally-gemini-app-mac-os/</link><media:content height="540" medium="image" url="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-uniblog-publish-prod/images/Gemini_for_macOS_language_capab.max-600x600.format-webp.webp" width="540"/><media:description>Gemini for macOS language capabilities</media:description><description>&lt;img src="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-uniblog-publish-prod/images/Gemini_for_macOS_language_capab.max-600x600.format-webp.webp"&gt;A look at how the Gemini app for macOS now lets you speak naturally to get clean transcriptions, edits, and summaries just using your voice.</description><pubDate>Wed, 29 Jul 2026 15:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/products/gemini-app/speak-naturally-gemini-app-mac-os/</guid><category>Gemini App</category><og xmlns:og="http://ogp.me/ns#"><type>article</type><title>Gemini for macOS adds new natural language capabilities</title><description>A look at how the Gemini app for macOS now lets you speak naturally to get clean transcriptions, edits, and summaries just using your voice.</description><site_name>Google</site_name><url>https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/products/gemini-app/speak-naturally-gemini-app-mac-os/</url></og><author xmlns:author="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><name>Michael Friedman</name><title>Group Product Manager</title><department>Gemini App</department><company/></author><author xmlns:author="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><name>Alvin Zhou</name><title>Senior Product Manager, Google DeepMind</title><department/><company/></author></item><item><title>How Gemini Flash agents are helping a Michigan dairy farmer</title><link>https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/models-and-research/gemini-models/using-gemini-to-manage-farm/</link><media:content height="540" medium="image" url="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-uniblog-publish-prod/images/Gemini_Flash_Michigan_dairy_far.max-600x600.format-webp.webp" width="540"/><media:description>Using Gemini to manage a farm</media:description><description>&lt;img src="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-uniblog-publish-prod/images/Gemini_Flash_Michigan_dairy_far.max-600x600.format-webp.webp"&gt;See how Paul Windemuller, a Michigan dairy farmer, is changing the way he works by using AI agents built with Gemini 3.6 Flash.</description><pubDate>Tue, 28 Jul 2026 16:15:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/models-and-research/gemini-models/using-gemini-to-manage-farm/</guid><category>Gemini models</category><og xmlns:og="http://ogp.me/ns#"><type>article</type><title>How Gemini Flash agents are helping a Michigan dairy farmer</title><description>See how Paul Windemuller, a Michigan dairy farmer, is changing the way he works by using AI agents built with Gemini 3.6 Flash.</description><site_name>Google</site_name><url>https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/models-and-research/gemini-models/using-gemini-to-manage-farm/</url></og><author xmlns:author="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><name>News from Google Team</name><title/><department/><company/></author></item><item><title>3 new ways nonprofits can put AI to work</title><link>https://blog.google/company-news/outreach-and-initiatives/google-org/nonprofits-ai-tools-training/</link><media:content height="540" medium="image" url="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-uniblog-publish-prod/images/Nonprofits_AI_hero_1.max-600x600.format-webp.webp" width="540"/><media:description>A man points to a computer screen. Another man smiles looking at the screen.</media:description><description>&lt;img src="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-uniblog-publish-prod/images/Nonprofits_AI_hero_1.max-600x600.format-webp.webp"&gt;We’re introducing new tools and resources for nonprofits to learn more about Google AI tools.</description><pubDate>Tue, 28 Jul 2026 16:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.google/company-news/outreach-and-initiatives/google-org/nonprofits-ai-tools-training/</guid><category>Google.org</category><og xmlns:og="http://ogp.me/ns#"><type>article</type><title>3 new ways nonprofits can put AI to work</title><description>We’re introducing new tools and resources for nonprofits to learn more about Google AI tools.</description><site_name>Google</site_name><url>https://blog.google/company-news/outreach-and-initiatives/google-org/nonprofits-ai-tools-training/</url></og><author xmlns:author="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><name>Maggie Johnson</name><title>Global Head</title><department>Google.org</department><company/></author></item><item><title>Gemini API Managed Agents: 3.6 Flash, hooks, and more</title><link>https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/technology/developers-tools/expanding-managed-agents-gemini-api-3-6-flash-hooks/</link><media:content height="540" medium="image" url="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-uniblog-publish-prod/images/unnamed_2_vNnOv20.max-600x600.format-webp.webp" width="540"/><media:description>Managed Agents Gemini 3.6 Flash, Hooks and Triggers</media:description><description>&lt;img src="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-uniblog-publish-prod/images/unnamed_2_vNnOv20.max-600x600.format-webp.webp"&gt;We’re announcing even more new capabilities in Managed Agents in Gemini API so developers can build reliable, production-ready agents.</description><pubDate>Tue, 28 Jul 2026 16:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/technology/developers-tools/expanding-managed-agents-gemini-api-3-6-flash-hooks/</guid><category>Developer tools</category><category>AI</category><og xmlns:og="http://ogp.me/ns#"><type>article</type><title>Gemini API Managed Agents: 3.6 Flash, hooks, and more</title><description>We’re announcing even more new capabilities in Managed Agents in Gemini API so developers can build reliable, production-ready agents.</description><site_name>Google</site_name><url>https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/technology/developers-tools/expanding-managed-agents-gemini-api-3-6-flash-hooks/</url></og><author xmlns:author="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><name>Philipp Schmid</name><title>Member of the Technical Staff</title><department>Google DeepMind</department><company/></author><author xmlns:author="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><name>Mariano Cocirio</name><title>Product Manager</title><department>Google DeepMind</department><company/></author></item><item><title>5 ways to host the ultimate dinner party with Google Search</title><link>https://blog.google/products-and-platforms/products/search/dinner-party-hosting-tips/</link><media:content height="540" medium="image" url="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-uniblog-publish-prod/images/Dinner_parties.max-600x600.format-webp.webp" width="540"/><media:description>An illustrated black magnifying glass with a sparkle in a white circle surrounded by a dinner party tablescape</media:description><description>&lt;img src="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-uniblog-publish-prod/images/Dinner_parties.max-600x600.format-webp.webp"&gt;These AI features can help you craft a menu, design a tablescape, and handle other party-planning tasks.</description><pubDate>Tue, 28 Jul 2026 13:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.google/products-and-platforms/products/search/dinner-party-hosting-tips/</guid><category>Search</category><category>AI</category><og xmlns:og="http://ogp.me/ns#"><type>article</type><title>5 ways to host the ultimate dinner party with Google Search</title><description>These AI features can help you craft a menu, design a tablescape, and handle other party-planning tasks.</description><site_name>Google</site_name><url>https://blog.google/products-and-platforms/products/search/dinner-party-hosting-tips/</url></og><author xmlns:author="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><name>News from Google Team</name><title/><department/><company/></author></item><item><title>These Google Trends show people really want to touch grass</title><link>https://blog.google/products-and-platforms/products/search/touch-grass-trends/</link><media:content height="540" medium="image" url="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-uniblog-publish-prod/images/Touch_Grass_Trends_hero.max-600x600.format-webp.webp" width="540"/><media:description>Illustration of a phone in do-not-disturb mode against green grass</media:description><description>&lt;img src="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-uniblog-publish-prod/images/Touch_Grass_Trends_hero.max-600x600.format-webp.webp"&gt;Google Search data reveals a growing desire to unplug and connect in real life with local run clubs, mahjong lessons and more.</description><pubDate>Tue, 28 Jul 2026 13:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.google/products-and-platforms/products/search/touch-grass-trends/</guid><category>Search</category><og xmlns:og="http://ogp.me/ns#"><type>article</type><title>These Google Trends show people really want to touch grass</title><description>Google Search data reveals a growing desire to unplug and connect in real life with local run clubs, mahjong lessons and more.</description><site_name>Google</site_name><url>https://blog.google/products-and-platforms/products/search/touch-grass-trends/</url></og><author xmlns:author="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><name>News from Google Team</name><title/><department/><company/></author></item><item><title>5 ways AI Mode in Search helps you enjoy the real world</title><link>https://blog.google/products-and-platforms/products/search/ai-mode-real-world-tips/</link><media:content height="540" medium="image" url="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-uniblog-publish-prod/images/AI_Mode_real_world.max-600x600.format-webp.webp" width="540"/><media:description>Illustration of a black magnifying glass in a white circle on green grass surrounded by items related to fun activities like tennis and games</media:description><description>&lt;img src="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-uniblog-publish-prod/images/AI_Mode_real_world.max-600x600.format-webp.webp"&gt;It might sound counterintuitive, but Search's AI tools can actually help you make the most of your time offline whether you want to book concert tickets or find the perf…</description><pubDate>Tue, 28 Jul 2026 13:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.google/products-and-platforms/products/search/ai-mode-real-world-tips/</guid><category>Search</category><category>AI</category><og xmlns:og="http://ogp.me/ns#"><type>article</type><title>5 ways AI Mode in Search helps you enjoy the real world</title><description>It might sound counterintuitive, but Search's AI tools can actually help you make the most of your time offline whether you want to book concert tickets or find the perfect hiking boots.</description><site_name>Google</site_name><url>https://blog.google/products-and-platforms/products/search/ai-mode-real-world-tips/</url></og><author xmlns:author="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><name>News from Google Team</name><title/><department/><company/></author></item></channel></rss>